coder › Changed `src/emitter.ts` on branch `fix/emitter-snapshot-emit`: `emit` now copies the listener list (`list.slice()`) before iterating, so every listener registered when `emit` began is called exactly once in registration order; removals (`off`, including the `once` wrapper's self-removal) only affect later emits, and additions (`on`) are only seen from the next emit. `off` already returned whether it removed anything and `emit` already returned the call count, so the fix preserves both — `emit` returns `snapshot.length`.

Commits:
- `0fcb686 Snapshot listeners in emit so removals during emit skip nothing`
- `fbf2c51 Cover self-removal, removal of others, add-during-emit, once, off and emit count`

Added 7 tests to `src/emitter.test.ts`: self-removing listener doesn't skip the next one; a listener removed by an earlier listener still runs this emit but not the next; added-during-emit runs only from next emit; `once` before an ordinary listener fires once without silencing it; `off` return values; `emit` return values (including 0 for unknown events); registration order.

